  "generated_text": "1. **Identify the pattern:**\n   We start by considering the sum of powers of cosines. Notice that:\n   \\[\n   \\cos^6 \\theta + \\cos^6 (90^\\circ - \\theta) = \\cos^6 \\theta + \\sin^6 \\theta\n   \\]\n   Using the identity \\(\\cos^2 \\theta + \\sin^2 \\theta = 1\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   \\cos^6 \\theta + \\sin^6 \\theta = 1 - 3 \\cos^2 \\theta \\sin^2 \\theta\n   \\]\n\n2. **Simplify the expression:**\n   We can rewrite the sum as:\n   \\[\n   \\sum_{\\theta = 0^\\circ}^{90^\\circ} \\cos^6 \\theta = \\frac{1}{2} \\sum_{\\theta = 0^\\circ}^{90^\\circ} (1 - 3 \\cos^2 \\theta \\sin^2 \\theta)\n   \\]\n\n3. **Evaluate the sum:**\n   The sum of \\(1\\) over \\(91\\) terms (from \\(0\\) to \\(90\\)) is \\(",
